<header><p class="st-kicker">republic · Anatolia and the Levant</p><h1 class="st-title">Syrian Arab Republic</h1><p class="st-meta">1961 CE – present · capital Damascus</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">The Syrian state since 1961, ruled for over five decades by the Ba'ath party and the Assad family, and transformed by civil war.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>After Syrian officers broke away from the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/united-arab-republic">United Arab Republic</a> in September 1961, the country took the name Syrian Arab Republic. A coup on 8 March 1963 brought the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/baath-party">Ba'ath</a> party to power, and a further coup in 1966 brought its radical wing.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hafez-al-assad">Hafez al-Assad</a> took power in 1970 and built a one-party state dominated by the army and security services, drawing heavily on his Alawite community. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/syria">Syria</a> lost the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/golan-heights">Golan Heights</a> to <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/kingdom-of-israel">Israel</a> in 1967, intervened in <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/lebanese-republic">Lebanon</a> from 1976 and crushed an Islamist uprising at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hama">Hama</a> in 1982. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bashar-al-assad">Bashar al-Assad</a> succeeded his father in 2000. Repression of protests in 2011 led to a civil war that killed hundreds of thousands and displaced half the population.</p><h2>To the present</h2><p>On 8 December 2024 a rebel offensive led by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hayat-tahrir-al-sham">Hayat Tahrir al-Sham</a> took <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/damascus">Damascus</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bashar-al-assad">Bashar al-Assad</a> fled to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russia">Russia</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ahmed-al-sharaa">Ahmed al-Sharaa</a> became interim president in 2025, leading a transitional government.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/syrian-arab-republic.jpg" alt="Syrian Arab Republic" width="320" height="213"><figcaption>Image: Modification by AnonMoos of PD image File:Flag of Syria (1930–1958, 1961–1963).svg (previous non-vector versions were by Coup de … · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Syria_(2025-).svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1961 CE – present</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/21st-century">21st century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>republic</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>bureaucratic</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Damascus</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Hafez al-Assad, Bashar al-Assad, Ahmed al-Sharaa</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Sunni Islam</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Arabic</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/syria">Syria</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Syria</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1994&amp;focus=syrian-arab-republic" aria-label="Syrian Arab Republic on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5607 962 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Syrian Arab Republic lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5927 1218L5811 1337M5927 1218L5927 1218"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5811 1337h0M5927 1218h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5927 1218h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5927 1218h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Damascus. <a href="/atlas?year=1994&amp;focus=syrian-arab-republic">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
